# owned by sys-apps/horcrux-core: the Horcrux server core (every install, headless included)
# ZFS root: the module is rebuilt with every dist-kernel update, in the same emerge transaction and before the new initramfs (a kernel update without it leaves
# a ZFS-root machine with an initramfs that has no zfs.ko, or none at all).
sys-fs/zfs rootfs dist-kernel
sys-fs/zfs-kmod dist-kernel
# the initramfs generator the dist-kernel installkernel hook runs
# -systemd (and no UKI): the classic installkernel hooks on BOTH inits, so a kernel is always /boot/vmlinuz-<ver> + initramfs-<ver>.img, the layout
# GRUB's generated config, horcrux-be and the installer use (with USE=systemd, kernel-install wrote /boot/kernel-<ver> on the systemd image)
sys-kernel/installkernel dracut -systemd -systemd-boot -uki -ukify
# the server core never needs a display stack: the hypervisor is managed through the web UI, the API and ssh (VM consoles are served as VNC/SPICE streams)
